@startuml
title SD2 : Reply received and consent applied

actor Recipient
participant "Channel Transport" as CT
participant "//Communication Interaction Management//" as CIM
participant "Party Privacy Management" as PPM
participant "Party Interaction Management" as PIM

Recipient -> CT : 1 replies "STOP" to the\norder-confirmation SMS
CT -> CIM : 2 inbound message "STOP"\n(on the SMS transport; no ODA interface)
activate CIM
note right of CIM
  No ODA component terminates this ingress today.
  Recorded in §5.2.
end note
CIM -> CIM : 3 recognise "STOP" as a consent keyword;\nassociate with the notification dispatched in SD-1 (I1)
CIM -> PPM : 4 **TMF644 Privacy Management** record the consent change\nfor Alice — marketing withdrawn\n(resource level — see Table 12)
activate PPM
PPM --> CIM : 5 **TMF644** 200 OK
deactivate PPM
note right of PPM
  Privacy Management masters the profile.
  Enforcement occurs at dispatch (X6).
end note
CIM -> PIM : 6 **TMF683 Party Interaction Management** POST /partyInteraction\n(direction="inbound", status="completed", channel[{name="sms"}],\nreason="STOP", relatedParty[{id="Alice"}],\ninteractionRelationship[{id=<the SD-1 interaction>,\nrelationshipType="replyTo"}])
activate PIM
PIM --> CIM : 7 **TMF683** 201 Created (id)
deactivate PIM
note right of PIM
  `direction` and `interactionRelationship` exist in
  TMF683 v4.0.0. The reply and its association with the
  preceding notification require no extension (I2).
end note
CIM -> CIM : 8 marketing to Alice now suppressed for every\nnotifying component; the regulatory and statutory\nclasses are unaffected (I3)
deactivate CIM

@enduml
